The Senate has 76 seats. Forty seats were up for election; six in each of the six states, two for the ACT and two for the Northern Territory. The terms of the four senators from the territories commenced on election day, all other terms take effect on 1 July 2014.<ref>Commonwealth of Australia Constitution Act, [http://www.austlii.edu.au/au/legis/cth/consol_act/coaca430/s13.html Section 13]. Retrieved 6 September 2010.</ref><ref>''Senate (Representation of Territories) Act'' 1973, [http://www.austlii.edu.au/au/legis/cth/num_act/sota1973408/s6.html Section 6. Retrieved August 2010.]</ref>

Senate results are provisional<ref>[http://www.abc.net.au/news/2013-09-09/senate-balance-of-power---who27s-who/4945390 Senate balance of power – Who's who: ABC 9 September 2013]</ref> with preference flows based on group voting tickets. The final result will not be known until a few weeks after the election. Provisional results indicate the [[Coalition (Australia)|Coalition]] government on 33 seats with the [[Australian Labor Party|Labor]] opposition on 25 seats. The [[Australian Greens|Greens]] are on 10 seats, and minor parties and independents on 8 seats – a total of 18 [[crossbencher]]s. The Coalition government would require the support of at least six non-coalition Senators to pass legislation.

The Motoring Enthusiast and Sports parties are on course to win a senate seat each, despite getting record-low primary votes of 0.50 percent in Victoria and 0.22 percent<ref name=VTRsenate/> in Western Australia respectively. The balance of their 14.3 percent quotas came from preference flows after cross-transfer agreements between multiple small parties. The larger parties, including the incoming government, are looking at changing the Senate voting system to prevent this.<ref>[http://www.businessspectator.com.au/news/2013/9/8/election/election-coalition-shy-senate-majority Coalition shy of Senate majority: Business Spectator 9 September 2013]</ref><ref>[http://www.watoday.com.au/federal-politics/federal-election-2013/tony-abbott-fires-a-warning-shot-at-micro-parties-in-the-senate-20130909-2tf5b.html Tony Abbott fires a warning shot at micro parties in the Senate: WA Today 9 September 2013]</ref><ref>[http://news.ninemsn.com.au/national/2013/09/09/08/50/xenophon-wants-voting-reform Xenophon wants voting reform: NineMSN 9 September 2013]</ref>

